<title>RUSSIA: Russia Uneximbank group says won Svyazinvest stake.</title>
<headline>Russia Uneximbank group says won Svyazinvest stake.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium including Russia's Uneximbank, its Bank MFK (ICFI) and Interros Group affiliates, Moscow investment bank Renaissance Capital, and Germany's Deutsche Bank AG won a tender for 25 percent plus one share in Russian telecoms holding company Svyazinvest with a bid of $1.8 billion, a spokesman for Uneximbank told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>There was no official confirmation from the organisers of the auction, the Russian Federal Property Fund, which had been due to release the results after 1300 GMT (5 p.m. local).</p>
</text>
